{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.Quotient","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHeckeAlgebra","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Matrix","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instReverseLimitQToInfinity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instReverseLimitQToInfinity","kind":"instance","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L195-L202","doc":"The carrier is inhabited at any nonzero `q` by the proved\nstructural identity — the conjecture's algebraic fragment is\nclosed, not assumed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity.bar_image_quadratic_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity.bar_image_quadratic_holds","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L191-L191","doc":"The bar-image structural identity holds for all `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L189-L189","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.ReverseLimitQToInfinity","kind":"class","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L182-L193","doc":"**Conjecture-closure carrier for `conj:reverse-limit-q-to-infinity`\n(algebraic fragment).** The single field encodes the bar-image\nstructural identity itself: under the bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` the\nHecke quadratic at `q⁻¹` equals `q⁻¹` times a re-scaling of the\nquadratic at `q`, for every `X`. An instance over a nonzero `q : R`\nis discharged from `reverse_limit_q_to_infinity_structural`; the\nfull categorical bar (canonical-basis level) is Sprint 5 scope. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:reverse-limit-q-to-infinity","label":"conj:reverse-limit-q-to-infinity","md":"quantum-observable-universe/stochastic-mechanics/reverse-limit-q-to-infinity.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.reverse_limit_q_to_infinity_structural","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.reverse_limit_q_to_infinity_structural","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L159-L173","doc":"**Discharge of `conj:reverse-limit-q-to-infinity` (algebraic\nfragment).** The bar involution `q ↦ q⁻¹` exchanges the Hecke\nquadratic relations at `q` and at `q⁻¹` up to multiplication\nby the unit `q⁻¹`. Hence the algebra `IwahoriHeckeOfSn R q⁻¹`\nis the bar-image of `IwahoriHeckeOfSn R q` at the level of\ndefining relations.\n\nThe full categorical bar (acting on the canonical basis) is\nSprint 5 scope. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.bar_image_hecke_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.bar_image_hecke_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":146,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L146-L157","doc":"**Bar-image of the Hecke quadratic at a unit `q`.** The\nquadratic `σ² - (q - 1) σ - q` transforms under `q ↦ q⁻¹`\ninto `σ² - (q⁻¹ - 1) σ - q⁻¹`, which equals `q⁻¹` times a\nre-scaling of the original quadratic.\n\nStated over a `Field R` (so `q⁻¹` exists when `q ≠ 0`); the\nframework's substrate `q_0 ≈ 1.11` is in this regime. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.isUnit_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.isUnit_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L120-L123","doc":"Each strand generator is invertible whenever `q` is, so `σ_i⁻¹` denotes an actual\nelement and the skein dictionary of §7a applies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.sigma_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.sigma_braid","kind":"theorem","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L114-L118","doc":"**The braid relation** holds — the half the old construction did not impose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.sigma_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.sigma_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L109-L112","doc":"**The Hecke quadratic relation** holds for every strand generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.σ","kind":"def","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L103-L105","doc":"**The strand-σ generator** `σ_i ∈ IwahoriHeckeOfSn R q n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instAlgebraIwahoriHeckeOfSn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instAlgebraIwahoriHeckeOfSn","kind":"instance","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L100-L101","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instRingIwahoriHeckeOfSn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.instRingIwahoriHeckeOfSn","kind":"instance","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L97-L98","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.IwahoriHeckeOfSn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.IwahoriHeckeOfSn","kind":"def","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L77-L95","doc":"**The type-A Iwahori–Hecke algebra** `H_n(q)`.\n\n**Rebuilt 2026-08-30.**  This read\n\n```\nnoncomputable def IwahoriHeckeOfSn : Type max 0 v :=\n  Quotient.IwahoriHeckeQuot R q (adjacentTranspositionIndex n)\n```\n\nThe *indexing* was right — `adjacentTranspositionIndex n` really is the simple\nreflections, unlike the generic `IwahoriHecke` which passed all of `W`.  What was\nmissing is the other half: `IwahoriHeckeQuot` imposes the **quadratic relation only**.\nThe object was therefore the free product of `n − 1` copies of `R[x]/((x−q)(x+1))`, in\nwhich no braid relation held.\n\nNow built on `QOU.MathlibExt.IwahoriHecke.HeckeAlgebra` at the type-A Coxeter matrix, so\nboth families hold. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.strandMatrix","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.strandMatrix","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L72-L75","doc":"**The type-A Coxeter matrix on the strand indices**, i.e. Mathlib's `CoxeterMatrix.Aₙ`\non `Fin (n - 1)`: adjacent strands braid (`m = 3`), distant ones commute (`m = 2`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.adjacentTranspositionIndex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.TypeA.adjacentTranspositionIndex","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean#L67-L70","doc":"The set of adjacent transpositions in `S_n`: `{(i, i+1) : 0 ≤ i < n-1}`,\nabstractly indexed by `Fin (n - 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}